3,"Embera Language and the Emberá Indian Tribe (Embera-Wounaan, Epena ...",https://www.native-languages.org/embera.htm,"Embera Indian Language (Emberá-Wounaan, Empera, Cholo, Pedea, Bedea) Embera is a Chocoan language of South America. Embera is spoken by around 80,000 people in Colombia and Panama. It has SOV word order. Sponsored Links Embera Language Resources Language map of Panama: Indigenous Northern Colombia: Maps showing the areas where the Embera dialects are spoken. Diccionario Embera: Online Spanish ...",Embera Baudó,Chocoan
